# Each `e_ach` (B6) applies a function to every item and keeps the
# shape. Scalar functions already apply item by item (T7); e_ach is for
# the rest, such as a function with a guard, whose condition must be a
# single value. Items are visited in order.
== SOURCE
'n_eg e_ach 1 2 3
u:s_ign := { x -> x < 0 ? -1; x = 0 ? 0; 1 }
'u:s_ign e_ach -5 0 7
'u:s_ign e_ach 2 2 r_eshape -1 0 1 2
'u:s_ign e_ach 4
t_ally 'u:s_ign e_ach 0 t_ake 1 2
'p_rint! e_ach 1 2
== TYPE
Int
u:s_ign : (Num a, Num b) => a -> b
Int
Int
Int
Int
Int
